# Cloudflare Pages _redirects: route rewrites (status 200) + redirects (3xx).
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# RFC 9727 says the catalog lives at /.well-known/api-catalog (no extension).
# Jekyll outputs the source file to /.well-known/api-catalog.json — rewrite the
# canonical path to the actual file. 200 = URL stays, content from new path.
/.well-known/api-catalog       /.well-known/api-catalog.json       200
/.well-known/api-onboarding    /.well-known/api-onboarding.json    200
/.well-known/agent-skills      /.well-known/agent-skills/index.json 200

# WARNING — this file is NOT honored on apievangelist.com as currently hosted.
# `_redirects` is a Cloudflare PAGES feature. This site serves from GitHub Pages
# behind the Cloudflare CDN (responses carry x-github-request-id with
# server: cloudflare), so nothing here is read at request time. The extensionless
# /.well-known/api-catalog 200 above comes from a Cloudflare-side rule, not from
# this file. Verified 2026-08-17 by adding a 301 here and getting a 404.
# Any new redirect has to be added as a Cloudflare Redirect Rule instead.
